  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>
    Balances alone do not explain whether someone has breathing room, and a
    generic checklist rarely shows what to address first. Cooked Finance turns
    seven estimates into four visible signals and a short list of next moves.
    It is designed to start a useful review—not to issue a verdict about a
    person or replace a financial plan.
  </p>

  <h2>What the financial health check measures</h2>
  <p>The current Cooked Score combines four narrowly defined pillars:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cash buffer (30%):</strong> liquid savings divided by essential monthly spending.</li>
    <li><strong>Debt burden (25%):</strong> required monthly debt payments divided by gross monthly income.</li>
    <li><strong>Savings habit (20%):</strong> monthly saving and investing divided by gross monthly income.</li>
    <li><strong>Long-term progress (25%):</strong> retirement investments compared with a broad age-based guidepost.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The formulas, weights, interpolation rules, sources, and limitations are
    published on the <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>. The score is
    not a credit score, population percentile, forecast, or statement of net
    worth.
  </p>

  <h2>Our publishing standards</h2>
  <p>
    We separate sourced facts from our own educational model, link to primary
    sources where practical, date material updates, and correct material errors.
    You can review the <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>,
    <a href="/source-policy/">source policy</a>, and
    <a href="/corrections-policy/">corrections policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Cooked Finance does not claim to be a financial adviser or fiduciary.
    Because finance is personal and the calculator sees only seven values,
    important context—including taxes, dependents, insurance, interest rates,
    projected defined-benefit pension income, location, goals, and risk tolerance—is outside the result.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy and funding</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Private by design:</strong> calculations run in the browser and financial inputs are not sent to our servers or analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>No account required:</strong> there is no login, bank connection, or database profile.</li>
    <li><strong>Currently ad-free:</strong> Cooked Finance has not applied for AdSense and displays no paid advertising.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Optional analytics load only after consent and never receive the seven
    calculator inputs or result values. Read the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>
    and <a href="/advertising-policy/">advertising policy</a> for details.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions, evidence, or corrections</h2>
  <p>
    If a formula is unclear, a source has changed, or a page contains an error,
    please use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Specific, verifiable
    feedback helps improve the site.
  </p>
